10. Bidirectional Teaching Protocol

The teaching channel \mathcal{T} carries two message types.

10.1 Mediator‑to‑Policy Signal

· primary_constraint_id: The constraint responsible for the largest correction.
· active_constraint_ids: Full list of constraints active in the current QP solve.
· InterventionLevel: A categorical severity label (NO\_INTERVENTION, MINOR, MAJOR, TRAJECTORY\_MOD, GOAL\_SUBSTITUTION).
· capability_preservation: Fraction of the AI’s original intent preserved after mediation, in [0,1].
· photonic_confidence: Inverse of the EKF covariance trace, in [0,1].

When photonic confidence is low, the teaching signal advises the policy to reduce velocity and increase compliance.

10.2 Policy‑to‑Mediator Signal

· TrustLevel \in \{\text{DISTRUST}, \text{NEUTRAL}, \text{HIGH\_TRUST}\} adjusts constraint margins.
· SofteningPermission: Temporary relaxation of a specific constraint, with a maximum allowable decoupling force.
· IntentPreview: Predicted future intents enabling the mediator to pre‑compute warm‑start information.

10.3 Policy Adaptation

The policy maintains a constraint violation prediction model \hat{P}_i = \sigma(\theta^T \phi_i) for each constraint. Upon receiving a teaching signal with actual violation indicator v_i \in \{0,1\}, the model is updated via online logistic regression:

\theta \leftarrow \theta - \eta (\hat{P}_i - v_i) \phi_i.

Under an i.i.d. context distribution, this converges to the true violation probabilities at rate O(1/\sqrt{T}).

