In hybrid joints, the QDD motor and the Halbach ring share the module endplate. The PCMSA coil provides fine‑motion stabilisation acting directly on the magnetic gap, while the QDD supplies the gross torque required for locomotion and heavy manipulation. This preserves the PCMSA’s cable‑free, backdrivable coupling in the proximal limbs while meeting the torque density demands that are beyond the current reach of Lorentz actuation alone.

